{"t": 1794115393.3884919, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "reports-api 502s \u2014 root cause found: upstream ledger 2026.11 added `currency` to every row, but reports/export.py built a csv.DictWriter with only `id,amount`, so every export raised `ValueError: dict contains fields not in fieldnames: 'currency'` and the request failed. Fixed in reports/export.py: `currency` is now included in the CSV and unknown future fields are ignored rather than crashing the export. Verified locally with current and legacy row shapes. Change still needs to be deployed to the reports-api ECS service to restore traffic."}, "ok": true}
